From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: tcdent <tcdent@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 19:15:25 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 16/38] rust: fs: fsnotify, page invalidation and dcache
 helpers

For a file system that learns of changes from somewhere other than the
VFS and has to report them the way the VFS would: INode::notify,
notify_dirent and notify_child wrap fsnotify() for the self, directory
entry and child-of-directory cases, with fs::notify holding the FS_*
bits. INode::invalidate_pages, INode::clear_nlink and
SuperBlock::shrink_dcache cover what such a file system does to its own
cached state when told about a change.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SKmspe5nVbuvzdvYZa9UhW
